1
00:00:00,657 --> 00:00:04,166
Managing the control flow of workflows is

2
00:00:04,198 --> 00:00:04,807
important.

3
00:00:05,544 --> 00:00:09,198
What's also important is to sometimes add a

4
00:00:09,246 --> 00:00:12,964
human in the loop because not all AI

5
00:00:13,076 --> 00:00:16,185
workflows or agents should run fully

6
00:00:16,522 --> 00:00:19,679
automatically. Or put in other words, just

7
00:00:19,743 --> 00:00:22,499
because you're building an AI workflow or

8
00:00:22,531 --> 00:00:26,281
agent does not mean that you need to blindly

9
00:00:26,313 --> 00:00:29,551
trust all its decisions and let it do its

10
00:00:29,679 --> 00:00:32,932
thing totally on its own. Of course, you can

11
00:00:33,189 --> 00:00:36,988
build workflows or agents that are 100%

12
00:00:37,196 --> 00:00:39,376
automated, which means that once the

13
00:00:39,441 --> 00:00:42,182
workflow started, it runs and finishes on

14
00:00:42,182 --> 00:00:44,715
its own. Maybe some initial input is

15
00:00:44,827 --> 00:00:47,327
required. We saw some examples for that

16
00:00:47,472 --> 00:00:49,764
throughout this section, but thereafter you

17
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:49,908
can

18
00:00:50,501 --> 00:00:53,788
lean back, relax, and you'll get a result at

19
00:00:53,788 --> 00:00:54,910
some point. And

20
00:00:55,471 --> 00:00:58,613
for many workflows, this is ideal. For

21
00:00:58,613 --> 00:01:01,386
example, that blog post generation workflow

22
00:01:01,418 --> 00:01:04,545
I just showed you, there we We just start

23
00:01:04,545 --> 00:01:07,465
the workflow with some input and thereafter

24
00:01:07,497 --> 00:01:11,042
no further input by us is required. And we

25
00:01:11,042 --> 00:01:14,139
can be perfectly happy with such a workflow

26
00:01:14,155 --> 00:01:16,160
and that might be exactly what we want.

27
00:01:16,802 --> 00:01:20,476
But we can also add a human in the loop and

28
00:01:21,069 --> 00:01:23,476
that may actually make a lot of sense

29
00:01:23,476 --> 00:01:26,652
depending on what your workflow or agent is

30
00:01:26,925 --> 00:01:27,214
doing.

31
00:01:27,871 --> 00:01:30,680
And human in the loop simply means that

32
00:01:31,097 --> 00:01:34,420
during execution, a workflow may require

33
00:01:34,549 --> 00:01:37,182
additional input or confirmation by the

34
00:01:37,182 --> 00:01:40,424
user. So not just initially, but also maybe

35
00:01:40,585 --> 00:01:44,165
sometime during the execution, possibly also

36
00:01:44,165 --> 00:01:46,846
multiple times. Again, it's your code, your

37
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:49,735
workflow. You decide how it works and when

38
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,871
input is required and when it isn't.

39
00:01:52,994 --> 00:01:54,841
For example, if you're building a workflow

40
00:01:55,242 --> 00:01:58,115
that automatically posts a suggested

41
00:01:58,228 --> 00:02:01,612
LinkedIn post to LinkedIn, you might want to

42
00:02:01,676 --> 00:02:05,171
add a step where you can check the suggested

43
00:02:05,363 --> 00:02:08,537
post and deny posting it if you're not happy

44
00:02:08,553 --> 00:02:08,857
with it.

45
00:02:09,675 --> 00:02:12,961
Or going back to this blog post generation

46
00:02:12,961 --> 00:02:16,632
example here, this is the same workflow as

47
00:02:16,744 --> 00:02:19,566
before, but I did now add a human in the

48
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:21,153
loop step to it.

49
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:24,631
And I added it because it's my workflow.

50
00:02:24,679 --> 00:02:28,446
It's my decision where I want user input and

51
00:02:28,446 --> 00:02:30,434
where I don't want user input. If you're

52
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:32,662
building your workflow, you decide at which

53
00:02:32,839 --> 00:02:36,510
point, if at all, you want extra user input.

54
00:02:37,263 --> 00:02:39,667
Of course, this workflow worked fine without

55
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:42,232
the input, but here I want to provide the

56
00:02:42,232 --> 00:02:44,268
user with an opportunity to

57
00:02:44,861 --> 00:02:46,432
share their own feedback

58
00:02:47,025 --> 00:02:49,975
on that article, to override the decision

59
00:02:50,392 --> 00:02:53,213
made by this evaluation step, essentially.

60
00:02:54,415 --> 00:02:56,852
And here I decided to give the user 3

61
00:02:57,124 --> 00:02:59,385
options. Again, because it's my workflow,

62
00:02:59,625 --> 00:03:02,030
that's my decision. I decided to give the

63
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:02,799
user 3 options.

64
00:03:03,955 --> 00:03:06,442
They can just hit enter, which means they

65
00:03:06,506 --> 00:03:08,320
will not provide their own feedback.

66
00:03:08,432 --> 00:03:11,754
Instead, they'll just accept the feedback

67
00:03:11,754 --> 00:03:14,756
generated by this evaluation step as it is.

68
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:18,463
If this step decided that no further

69
00:03:18,479 --> 00:03:19,522
improvement is needed,

70
00:03:20,228 --> 00:03:22,620
the workflow will continue like before. It

71
00:03:22,652 --> 00:03:24,979
will exit out of the loop and the next steps

72
00:03:25,059 --> 00:03:25,621
will start.

73
00:03:26,407 --> 00:03:28,751
If the evaluation step did decide that

74
00:03:28,751 --> 00:03:30,901
improvement is needed, it'll go ahead and

75
00:03:30,901 --> 00:03:33,549
regenerate that article. So if the user hits

76
00:03:33,629 --> 00:03:36,005
Enter, everything will work just as before

77
00:03:36,277 --> 00:03:38,251
without that human feedback step here.

78
00:03:39,166 --> 00:03:41,397
But that changes if the user enters the word

79
00:03:41,493 --> 00:03:41,991
accept.

80
00:03:42,793 --> 00:03:45,345
Because if the user does this, then we

81
00:03:45,361 --> 00:03:47,415
accept the article as is

82
00:03:48,073 --> 00:03:50,705
and we overwrite any suggested changes.

83
00:03:51,524 --> 00:03:54,958
So even if this evaluation step decided that

84
00:03:55,135 --> 00:03:57,622
further improvement is needed, if the user

85
00:03:57,638 --> 00:04:01,457
enters accept, we discard this and we exit

86
00:04:01,554 --> 00:04:04,105
out of the loop and accept the article draft

87
00:04:04,281 --> 00:04:04,987
as it is.

88
00:04:06,303 --> 00:04:08,485
And the last option is that the user enters

89
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:11,598
their own feedback, which also overrides the

90
00:04:12,064 --> 00:04:15,417
evaluation step result because now we always

91
00:04:15,770 --> 00:04:18,626
request another iteration. We request a new

92
00:04:18,819 --> 00:04:21,001
draft and we overwrite whatever this

93
00:04:21,001 --> 00:04:22,558
evaluation step gave us.

94
00:04:23,392 --> 00:04:25,735
And here's the actual logic for implementing

95
00:04:25,783 --> 00:04:25,943
this.

96
00:04:26,585 --> 00:04:28,527
I'm checking whether the user entered

97
00:04:28,527 --> 00:04:31,701
accept, in which case we always set needs

98
00:04:31,734 --> 00:04:34,297
improvement to false even if it was true

99
00:04:34,297 --> 00:04:34,569
before,

100
00:04:35,419 --> 00:04:37,389
which means we'll always make it out of this

101
00:04:37,501 --> 00:04:39,520
loop. We'll always continue with the next

102
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,449
steps thereafter.

103
00:04:41,651 --> 00:04:43,622
If that's not met, we check if the user

104
00:04:43,814 --> 00:04:46,169
entered any feedback. So if they submitted a

105
00:04:46,169 --> 00:04:49,246
non-empty message, in that case, we also

106
00:04:49,278 --> 00:04:51,697
override the evaluation result and we always

107
00:04:51,697 --> 00:04:53,924
set it to true and we take that user

108
00:04:53,924 --> 00:04:56,423
feedback as a feedback for the next

109
00:04:56,423 --> 00:04:59,147
iteration cycle, for the next draft version.

110
00:04:59,773 --> 00:05:02,617
And if the user enters nothing, then neither

111
00:05:02,649 --> 00:05:04,978
of these conditions is met and the workflow

112
00:05:04,978 --> 00:05:06,392
continued as it was before.

113
00:05:06,922 --> 00:05:09,589
Now here for me, it will still stop after 3

114
00:05:09,589 --> 00:05:11,903
cycles, even if the user did enter extra

115
00:05:11,903 --> 00:05:14,088
feedback. Of course, you could adjust the

116
00:05:14,152 --> 00:05:16,305
loop to make sure that if the user entered

117
00:05:16,305 --> 00:05:18,281
their own feedback, this condition here

118
00:05:18,394 --> 00:05:19,004
doesn't count.

119
00:05:20,081 --> 00:05:22,250
For example, if you adjusted it like this,

120
00:05:22,410 --> 00:05:25,367
you would make sure that the loop is only

121
00:05:25,415 --> 00:05:29,297
stopped If we have more than 3 cycles and

122
00:05:30,035 --> 00:05:32,585
we don't have any user feedback. If we do

123
00:05:32,698 --> 00:05:35,007
have user feedback, we'll continue even if

124
00:05:35,007 --> 00:05:36,996
we're above those 3 cycles.

125
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:39,338
But that's something that's totally up to

126
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:39,450
you.

127
00:05:40,156 --> 00:05:40,813
And with that,

128
00:05:41,519 --> 00:05:44,406
I can of course again run this project here,

129
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:46,154
this workflow

130
00:05:46,892 --> 00:05:49,282
based on my AI workflows versus agents

131
00:05:49,362 --> 00:05:51,832
outline. And it will now go ahead and again

132
00:05:52,089 --> 00:05:54,479
generate a new article draft, of course.

133
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:57,429
And then once that's done, it will again

134
00:05:57,943 --> 00:06:00,524
create this automated evaluation. That

135
00:06:00,524 --> 00:06:03,106
doesn't change, but thereafter I'll get an

136
00:06:03,154 --> 00:06:05,367
opportunity to provide my own feedback.

137
00:06:06,314 --> 00:06:09,537
So here the automated evaluation step

138
00:06:09,729 --> 00:06:12,215
actually did decide that further improvement

139
00:06:12,231 --> 00:06:14,717
is needed, and this is the AI-generated

140
00:06:14,717 --> 00:06:15,069
feedback.

141
00:06:15,984 --> 00:06:18,549
But now I have a chance of hitting Enter to

142
00:06:18,549 --> 00:06:20,810
accept this decision by the evaluation

143
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:21,067
model.

144
00:06:21,997 --> 00:06:24,435
Enter accept to instead accept the article

145
00:06:24,643 --> 00:06:26,968
or enter my own feedback like should be

146
00:06:26,968 --> 00:06:27,369
shorter.

147
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:29,422
Or of course I could also enter more.

148
00:06:30,672 --> 00:06:32,917
Here I actually wanna accept the article as

149
00:06:32,917 --> 00:06:35,194
it is, so I'll enter the word accept and I

150
00:06:35,387 --> 00:06:37,616
override the decision by this evaluation

151
00:06:37,664 --> 00:06:39,684
step and therefore we now continue with

152
00:06:39,877 --> 00:06:42,523
thumbnail generation and LinkedIn post

153
00:06:42,523 --> 00:06:43,148
generation.

154
00:06:44,543 --> 00:06:46,483
And that's therefore an example for a

155
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:49,257
human-in-the-loop step in this example

156
00:06:49,354 --> 00:06:49,819
workflow.
